{"type":"message","id":"8d3a8d80","parentId":"f16859bf","timestamp":"2026-02-18T16:27:37.667Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-02-18 21:57 GMT+5:30] Build a deep search toolkit consisting of four OpenClaw skills:\n\n1. osint-crawl: Web crawling/scraping skill (use node-fetch or axios, respect robots.txt, rate limiting). Capture page content, extract links, and output structured JSON.\n\n2. osint-analyze: Analysis skill that takes crawled data (JSON) and produces insights: keyword extraction, sentiment, entity recognition, and summary.\n\n3. osint-youtube: YouTube search skill using YouTube Data API v3 (requires API key). Search videos, fetch metadata (title, description, views, likes, comments count), and return results.\n\n4. osint-search-multi: Orchestrator skill that can search multiple sources (web, YouTube, social) and aggregate results with deduplication.\n\nEach skill should:\n- Have its own directory under `skills/` with package.json, main file, README.md\n- Include example usage and test data\n- Be ready for integration via `skills.entries` in openclaw.json\n\nDeliver a comprehensive README at `skills/README.md` explaining how to install, configure (API keys for YouTube), and use each skill.\n\nWork step-by-step; report progress and any blockers. ETA: 1 hour."}],"timestamp":1771432057662}}
